    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green. Note the specific test (`coreRejectionIsProblemJson`) removes `city`, which is `@NotNull`, so it actually flows through the bean-validation `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler (400) \u2014 which now emits `application/problem+json` too.\n\n## Summary\n\nAll rejection responses (400, 409, 429) now return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`; status codes are unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`RestApiRejectionException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying an `HttpStatus` + detail message. Controllers throw this to reject a request instead of returning a bare status.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`**\n   - Added `@ExceptionHandler(RestApiRejectionException.class)` \u2192 builds a `ProblemDetail` (`type`, `title` = status reason phrase, `status`, `detail`) and returns it with an explicit `Content-Type: application/problem+json`.\n   - Set `application/problem+json` on the existing bean-validation (400) `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler as well, since it's also a rejection path.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced every bare `new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST / CONFLICT / TOO_MANY_REQUESTS)` in `addOwner`/`updateOwner` with a `throw new RestApiRejectionException(status, detail)` carrying a meaningful detail message, so they render through the central RFC7807 handler.\n\nTest suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
